{"name":"Daisy Desi","hex":"#fcdf8a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"daisy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wild flowering plant of species Bellis perennis of the family Asteraceae, with a yellow head and white petals","Any of numerous other flowering plants of various species, mostly among the asterids."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/daisy"},{"term":"desi","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative form of Desi."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Desi.","A particular variety of cultivated chickpea."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desi"}],"entries":[{"title":"Desi","blocks":[{"text":"Desi, also Deshi, is a loose term used to describe the peoples, cultures, and products of the Indian subcontinent and their diaspora, derived from Sanskrit देश, meaning 'land' or 'country'. Desi traces its origin to the people from the South Asian republics of India, Pakistan, and Bangladesh, and may also sometimes be extended to include Afghanistan, Bhutan, Maldives, Nepal, and Sri Lanka."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Location_of_Indian_Subcontinent.svg/330px-Location_of_Indian_Subcontinent.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desi"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Buckeye_Mela_IX_-_Spartan_Bhangra.jpg/500px-Buckeye_Mela_IX_-_Spartan_Bhangra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Buckeye_Mela_IX_-_Spartan_Bhangra.jpg/1280px-Buckeye_Mela_IX_-_Spartan_Bhangra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Buckeye_Mela_IX_-_Spartan_Bhangra.jpg/500px-Buckeye_Mela_IX_-_Spartan_Bhangra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai